# Destination hosts the agent container is allowed to reach.
#
# One pattern per line, fnmatch syntax (`*` and `?` wildcards). Matched against
# the host of every request -- including the host in a CONNECT, which is how
# HTTPS goes through a proxy. Anything not listed here is refused with 403 and
# logged. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#
# A pattern must match the ENTIRE hostname. `theguardian.com` therefore does
# *not* cover `www.theguardian.com` -- you need the wildcard form as well. This
# is the most common surprise here, and the proxy log names the exact host it
# refused, so read it there rather than guessing.
#
# Two ways to apply an edit:
#   fast   cp this file to ~/agent-sandbox/allowlist (oc.sh bind-mounts that
#          over the baked-in copy), then: podman restart agent-proxy
#   baked  podman build -f Dockerfile.proxy -t agent-egress-proxy:1 .
#          then: oc-proxy-down && oc

# The inference endpoint. Without this, nothing works.
api.inference.cscs.ch

# opencode's model catalogue, fetched at startup. Blocking it is survivable --
# the CSCS models are declared in the image config, not discovered -- but it
# logs an error on every start.
models.opencode.ai

# Uncomment if you want the agent to be able to clone or fetch from GitHub.
# Note this is also a plausible exfiltration route: a repo it can push to is a
# repo it can write your source into.
# github.com
# codeload.github.com
# objects.githubusercontent.com

# opencode asks npm for the provider SDK on the first message. It does NOT need
# the answer -- @ai-sdk/anthropic is compiled into the binary and it falls back
# to that -- so this stays commented out. Uncomment only if you add a provider
# whose SDK is genuinely not bundled. See "Pre-warming the provider SDK".
# registry.npmjs.org

# News sites, for the "can it reach the web?" demo. Both forms are needed: the
# apex on its own line, the wildcard for www., amp., rss. and friends.
theguardian.com
*.theguardian.com

# Uncomment to let the same demo reach CNN as well -- www.cnn.com, rss.cnn.com
# and edition.cnn.com are all covered by the wildcard.
# cnn.com
# *.cnn.com
